WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.939
We have yet another very important Supreme
Court decision, the Supreme Court has ruled

00:00:04.939 --> 00:00:09.700
that Donald Trump cannot shut down Dacca.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.559
And this is an important decision to understand
both because of what it does say and because

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:16.460
of what it doesn't say, actually.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.779
So as a reminder, DACA is Deferred Action
for Childhood Arrivals.

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:26.880
The idea is that there are people who came
to the United States illegally when they were

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:27.880
under age.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.630
They were not adults and they were brought
by parents.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:38.900
And DACA is essentially a program which says
we are not going to deport individuals who,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.870
even if they are adults today, as some of
them are, came here when they were children,

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.140
not by their choice, not because they said,
I'm going to do something which I know is

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.720
against the law, but because they were brought
here by their parents.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.100
And it's a completely logical program.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.390
And Donald Trump promised it's another failed
promise Donald Trump promised when he was

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.220
running for president back in 2015 and 2016.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:07.030
He said he would, quote, immediately terminate
the executive order by former President Barack

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:14.860
Obama, which he called illegal amnesty for
hundreds of thousands of young immigrants.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:20.810
About 700000 folks, in fact, potentially would
be affected by terminating DACA.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.539
And the Supreme Court has decided it's not
happening.

00:01:23.539 --> 00:01:25.729
But the devil is in the details.

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:29.049
And the reason why the Supreme Court decided
this is very important.

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:31.219
It was a five to four decision.

00:01:31.219 --> 00:01:36.770
Chief Justice John Roberts, a George W. Bush
appointee, wrote the majority opinion, along

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:41.450
with the four more liberal members of the
Supreme Court.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:47.749
And they wrote in that decision, quote, We
do not decide whether Dacca or its recision

00:01:47.749 --> 00:01:49.670
are sound policies.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:56.260
We address only whether the agency complied
with the procedural requirement that it provide

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.229
a reasoned explanation for its action.

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:02.979
So this is like the most important thing to
know.

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:07.719
The court is not deciding whether or not the
policy is good or bad.

00:02:07.719 --> 00:02:15.060
And the court is not deciding whether there
are other cases Trump could make to end Dacca.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.810
All the court is saying is that Trump's argument
was a bad one.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:25.000
Incredibly, this again comes down to the Trump
administration is sort of incompetent.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.690
The way they are making some of these legal
fights go is setting them up to lose.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:38.500
Donald Trump's argument was that when Barack
Obama created and maintained the program,

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.100
he was operating beyond the legal power he
has as president.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.700
That was the argument that was made.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:49.720
The Supreme Court looks at the argument that
is made and the Supreme Court decided no.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:56.170
Barack Obama had the power to do this and
he articulated reasons why he did it.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:00.680
And we aren't deciding whether we believe
politically they are good or bad reasons or

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.150
economically they are good or bad reasons.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.110
Trump's argument was Trump.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:09.930
Obama overstepped authority and the Supreme
Court determined that that is not the case.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:18.430
This should be a warning to us that Donald
Trump could try to revoke Dacca again and

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.900
formulate the argument differently.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:26.650
Donald Trump, if he were better and his lawyers
were better at filing documents, essentially

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.220
they could have made an argument that the
Supreme Court very well may have upheld and

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:34.000
said, go ahead and end DACA.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.221
So this is another reminder of how urgent
and important it is to remove Donald Trump

00:03:39.221 --> 00:03:42.780
in November before he can appoint more people
to the Supreme Court.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.800
And before he can again make what will probably
be a stronger legal argument, what could be

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.520
a stronger legal argument for ending DACA.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:56.350
Now, there are a couple of people writing
to me and I see them posting on Twitter and

00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:01.490
elsewhere saying, you idiot leftists who think
you've got to vote for Biden because of the

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.050
Supreme Court.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:09.410
Look at this Supreme Court which made the
decision you guys want on LGBT discrimination

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.530
last week.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:15.710
And now they made the decision that you want
on the issue of DACA this time around.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:21.229
The argument they are saying that we must
vote Biden over Trump because of the Supreme

00:04:21.229 --> 00:04:26.990
Court is a dumb argument, they say, because
the Supreme Court decided the way we would

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.419
have decided on these two cases.

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:32.080
And there's a couple of really important things
to point out here.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:39.419
Number one, the way that this ended up going
Obama's way on DACA rather than Trump's is

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:42.400
because Trump's argument was a dumb argument.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.280
It was just a bad legal argument.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.419
There's a very good.

00:04:45.419 --> 00:04:52.850
It was such a dumb argument that even a conservative
Supreme Court had to find this as the outcome.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:56.849
And remember, Gorsuch and Cavenagh both said,
yeah.

00:04:56.849 --> 00:04:58.780
This is a good enough argument to get rid
of DACA.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:04:59.780
So if.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:04.110
Donald Trump was able to put together a better
argument on getting rid of DACA.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.689
It would probably be gone right now.

00:05:05.689 --> 00:05:08.229
There's a good chance that it would have been
it would be gone right now.

00:05:08.229 --> 00:05:09.229
That's number one.

00:05:09.229 --> 00:05:10.400
Number two.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:14.490
The LGBT decision did go the right way.

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:18.009
But Kavanagh was wrong on that one.

00:05:18.009 --> 00:05:23.729
Another Kate Kavanagh voted with the minority
on the LGBT decision.

00:05:23.729 --> 00:05:28.910
And so did Gorsuch on on an and Gorsuch on
this one, along with Cavenagh.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:34.659
So the idea that we don't have to worry about
the Supreme Court because these two decisions

00:05:34.659 --> 00:05:39.669
went what we consider to be the right way
is an absolute and total joke.

00:05:39.669 --> 00:05:44.479
Only one of Trump's picks made the right decision
on one of these two cases.

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:47.000
Otherwise, you're talking about appointees
from other presidents.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:52.090
So if you're saying we don't need to worry
about judges in thinking about Biden versus

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:55.409
Trump 2020, you're living in a fantasy world.

00:05:55.409 --> 00:05:59.969
You're living on a planet that I certainly
don't don't recognize.

00:05:59.969 --> 00:06:04.370
And if anything, these two cases, when you
really look at the details, reinforce the

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:10.219
case for judges in the Supreme Court being
of critical importance in what we do in November.

